1
00:00:01,830 --> 00:00:04,413
(thunder clap)

2
00:00:05,798 --> 00:00:08,881
(audience applause)

3
00:00:15,323 --> 00:00:17,490
- [Alan] So now I don't have
to get struck by lightning,

4
00:00:17,490 --> 00:00:20,708
Fran's shown you what happens.

5
00:00:20,708 --> 00:00:22,532
So I'm gonna follow on from that.

6
00:00:22,532 --> 00:00:24,878
All right, 'cause I get
asked similar questions,

7
00:00:24,878 --> 00:00:28,157
I get asked like "Dear Evil
Tester", emails come into me,

8
00:00:28,157 --> 00:00:30,056
our Agile project is screwed up

9
00:00:30,056 --> 00:00:32,405
and messed up, what can I do?

10
00:00:32,405 --> 00:00:33,906
All right, 'cause people want to fix it,

11
00:00:33,906 --> 00:00:35,796
people want to take
responsibility for that.

12
00:00:35,796 --> 00:00:38,100
Where screwed up means some of the things

13
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:39,209
that Fran just talked about.

14
00:00:39,209 --> 00:00:43,617
Where we've got no time
for testing by the testers.

15
00:00:43,617 --> 00:00:48,086
We've got no time for
automating by the testers.

16
00:00:48,086 --> 00:00:51,680
We've got no acceptance criteria
that the testers can use.

17
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:53,566
We've got no story details that we

18
00:00:53,566 --> 00:00:56,269
as testers can understand,
we're not invited to meetings,

19
00:00:56,269 --> 00:00:58,245
and so the tester's not being included,

20
00:00:58,245 --> 00:01:00,579
we're not getting stuff we want.

21
00:01:00,579 --> 00:01:02,046
And the fundamental problem is

22
00:01:02,046 --> 00:01:03,900
that you're not actually Agile,

23
00:01:03,900 --> 00:01:05,621
you're not actually
doing an Agile project.

24
00:01:05,621 --> 00:01:07,709
You've called it Agile,
you've labelled it Agile,

25
00:01:07,709 --> 00:01:09,580
you've got some ritual
that you call Agile,

26
00:01:09,580 --> 00:01:12,028
you do stand-ups, you do retrospectives

27
00:01:12,028 --> 00:01:13,511
but you don't learn from them.

28
00:01:13,511 --> 00:01:17,832
The feedback doesn't come in
as input and you process it.

29
00:01:17,832 --> 00:01:19,909
So what we have to do
then is we still have to

30
00:01:19,909 --> 00:01:22,394
fight the good fight and
explain what Agile is

31
00:01:22,394 --> 00:01:24,860
and try and do the Agile thing.

32
00:01:24,860 --> 00:01:27,279
But we still have to work
with the actual reality

33
00:01:27,279 --> 00:01:31,174
on the ground so there are
steps that people can take.

34
00:01:31,174 --> 00:01:32,007
The first thing we have to do is

35
00:01:32,007 --> 00:01:34,469
we have to get our own house in order.

36
00:01:34,469 --> 00:01:37,006
Make sure that we know how to test things,

37
00:01:37,006 --> 00:01:39,427
make sure that we are avoiding waste in

38
00:01:39,427 --> 00:01:41,084
the testing that we do.

39
00:01:41,084 --> 00:01:42,892
So that we're not writing big test plans,

40
00:01:42,892 --> 00:01:44,993
we're not writing huge
amounts of stuff in advance,

41
00:01:44,993 --> 00:01:46,427
we're keeping everything lean

42
00:01:46,427 --> 00:01:49,396
so that we can respond effectively.

43
00:01:49,396 --> 00:01:52,383
We need to make sure that we do own

44
00:01:52,383 --> 00:01:54,705
the things that are ours to own.

45
00:01:54,705 --> 00:01:57,782
So exploratory testing, that
we make sure that we do that.

46
00:01:57,782 --> 00:02:00,428
That we do that properly,
we capture all the results

47
00:02:00,428 --> 00:02:01,914
and we plan it in advance.

48
00:02:01,914 --> 00:02:04,233
One of the things you
can do is you can use

49
00:02:04,233 --> 00:02:08,003
the Agile words against
the fake Agile process.

50
00:02:08,003 --> 00:02:10,514
So Agile has words like done, not done,

51
00:02:10,514 --> 00:02:12,179
so when you're planning out your testing,

52
00:02:12,179 --> 00:02:13,727
your exploratory testing,
and build charters,

53
00:02:13,727 --> 00:02:15,571
whatever lightweight plan you want to do,

54
00:02:15,571 --> 00:02:18,156
you say not done, then
you listen to things

55
00:02:18,156 --> 00:02:19,362
that you want to do.

56
00:02:19,362 --> 00:02:20,901
Then when you start doing them

57
00:02:20,901 --> 00:02:22,287
you gather evidence you say done,

58
00:02:22,287 --> 00:02:24,113
then you put them into a done list.

59
00:02:24,113 --> 00:02:26,085
So then at the end when people try and go,

60
00:02:26,085 --> 00:02:27,937
"can we close this story now? can we mark

61
00:02:27,937 --> 00:02:30,764
the story as done?", in
their face there's feedback,

62
00:02:30,764 --> 00:02:32,526
that it is not yet done,

63
00:02:32,526 --> 00:02:34,643
'cause there's a bunch of stuff not done

64
00:02:34,643 --> 00:02:36,064
and you're making it visible.

65
00:02:36,064 --> 00:02:37,928
You're helping people understand and share

66
00:02:37,928 --> 00:02:40,375
the pain that you've got.

67
00:02:40,375 --> 00:02:42,733
The other thing we have
to do, and this is,

68
00:02:42,733 --> 00:02:45,089
why we get in a mess because
in Agile you are supposed

69
00:02:45,089 --> 00:02:46,951
to do the work of other people as well,

70
00:02:46,951 --> 00:02:49,157
you are supposed to absorb things.

71
00:02:49,157 --> 00:02:50,488
But that's what we have to not do,

72
00:02:50,488 --> 00:02:51,894
you have to focus on the work that we do,

73
00:02:51,894 --> 00:02:55,422
and not absorb the poor
output from other things.

74
00:02:55,422 --> 00:02:57,617
So testers do not stay
late testing because

75
00:02:57,617 --> 00:03:01,558
the story was delivered at
four o'clock in the afternoon,

76
00:03:01,558 --> 00:03:03,098
while everyone else goes home.

77
00:03:03,098 --> 00:03:08,015
If we absorb things, then we
help this bad process continue

78
00:03:09,038 --> 00:03:11,445
and in a normal Agile
process you would want

79
00:03:11,445 --> 00:03:13,164
to help out, you want to make it work,

80
00:03:13,164 --> 00:03:15,136
but you're not in an Agile process.

81
00:03:15,136 --> 00:03:16,874
We have to work with the reality,

82
00:03:16,874 --> 00:03:19,807
and that means making
people share the pain,

83
00:03:19,807 --> 00:03:22,172
making this stuff visible.

84
00:03:22,172 --> 00:03:25,195
We have to give them a
reason to want to change,

85
00:03:25,195 --> 00:03:28,093
because the system has to change itself.

86
00:03:28,093 --> 00:03:31,012
We can only act on small things.

87
00:03:31,012 --> 00:03:32,579
Thank you very much.

88
00:03:32,579 --> 00:03:35,579
(audience applause)

